 4. ✊ Chart du jour: Socialism rising 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : Gallup. Chart: Neal Rothschild/Axios Americans' views of socialism have reached a record high, with 43% saying they view it positively, Axios' Neal Rothschild writes from a new Gallup poll . 

 Why it matters: President Trump has called democratic socialists the "biggest threat to our nation." But congressional Republican candidates are being warned that socialism isn't a strong attack line. 💥 By the numbers: The share of Americans who feel positively about socialism jumped from 39% to 43% in the past year.

 That shift came entirely from independents: positive views of socialism rose 8 points among that group since last year, to 45%. Reality check: Socialism remains less popular than capitalism, which 55% of Americans view positively.

