 5. 🪖 Trump asked Xi to stop supporting Iran 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump and first lady Melania Trump host President Xi Jinping of China and his wife, Peng Liyuan, for a morning tea at the White House Red Room yesterday. Photo: Doug Mills/The New York Times President Trump asked Chinese President Xi Jinping to halt any assistance to Iran when the two spoke during the state visit, U.S. Ambassador to China David Perdue told CNBC's "Squawk Box" yesterday.

 Why it matters: China's economic, intelligence and military support for Iran has undermined Trump's effort to isolate the country amid the ongoing war. The U.S. is conducting a massive economic pressure campaign against Iran. But without Chinese cooperation, it'll only be partially effective, Axios' Barak Ravid reports. The other side: According to Chinese state media , Xi urged Trump to de-escalate with Iran by returning to the June memorandum of understanding and reaching a nuclear deal.

 Read on . Via Truth Social Trump last night posted a map of the Middle East with the Strait of Hormuz relabeled as "TRUMP STRAIT," joining a presidential fantasy map collection that this month has included New Mexico as "New America" plus all of North America as part of the U.S. ( extending to Greenland and Iceland).

 
 
