 6. 🏛️ Senators spending the most on flights 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Sen. Mike Rounds (R-S.D.) has spent more taxpayer money on travel than any other senator's office since the fall of 2024 — including $625,000 on private charter companies, according to an analysis of public disclosures provided to Axios' Stef W. Kight. 

 Why it matters: Senators routinely fly between Washington and their home states on taxpayers' dime. But only a handful regularly rely on private flights. 🔎 Between the lines: Many senators with the biggest travel bills live in remote or large states, where there can be fewer commercial flight options home and longer routes to visit constituents across the state.

 There had been no flights leaving Pierre, S.D., that worked with the Senate schedule. So Rounds took chartered flights to Minnesota before flying commercial, with approval from the Senate Rules Committee, a spokesperson told Axios. Share this story . 

 
 
